+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report: `similar` 3.1.1
+
+Property-based tests were added with [hegel](https://hegel.dev) (`hegeltest`
+0.28.2) to the existing inline unit-test areas of the crate (no separate
+test files; there was no pre-existing proptest/quickcheck/fuzz setup to
+port). `cargo add --dev hegeltest` required `--ignore-rust-version`
+(`similar` pins `rust-version = "1.85"`, hegeltest needs 1.86) — if these
+tests are upstreamed, that dev-dependency MSRV is a maintainer decision.
+
+All properties run against **all five algorithms** (Myers, Patience, Lcs,
+Hunt, Histogram). Shared generators live in
+`src/common.rs::pbt_support` (byte-sequence pairs over a drawn small
+alphabet, `b` either independent or an edited copy of `a`, sometimes >100
+elements to hit the `IdentifyDistinct` path) and `src/text/mod.rs::pbt`
+(full-Unicode text pairs, identical pairs, and line-structured text with
+`\n`/`\r\n` terminators and optional missing final newline).
+
+## Properties tested
+
+Ten distinct properties, plus two deterministic "known failure" tests that
+pin the real bug found (next section):
+
+1. **Diff-then-apply roundtrip** (crown property; `src/common.rs`,
+   `hegel_capture_diff_apply_roundtrip`). For generated `a`, `b`, applying
+   the ops from `capture_diff_slices` to `a` (Equal content from `a`,
+   Insert/Replace content from `b` by index) reconstructs `b` exactly, for
+   every algorithm. This is simultaneously the algorithm-independence
+   check: all five algorithms must reconstruct `b` even though their op
+   sequences differ.
+
+2. **Op-sequence well-formedness** (`src/common.rs`,
+   `hegel_ops_partition_both_inputs`). The ops partition both inputs: old
+   ranges tile `0..a.len()`, new ranges tile `0..b.len()`, in order, no
+   gaps/overlaps. Evidence: existing unit tests
+   `test_compact_keeps_diffop_cursors_contiguous`,
+   `test_regression_issue_95`.
+
+3. **Equal ops are actually equal + no fully-empty ops**
+   (`src/common.rs`, `hegel_equal_ops_reference_equal_slices`). Every
+   `Equal` op names slices that compare equal; no op has both ranges
+   empty. *Found the Lcs/Hunt empty-input bug.*
+
+4. **Self-diff is all-Equal with ratio 1.0** (`src/common.rs`,
+   `hegel_self_diff_is_all_equal`), over the full `u8` alphabet. *Found
+   the same bug independently.*
+
+5. **Grouping preserves the op set** (`src/common.rs`,
+   `hegel_grouped_ops_preserve_changes`). `group_diff_ops(ops, n)` keeps
+   exactly the original non-Equal ops in order, and replaying the groups
+   over `a` (copying elided gaps from `a`) reconstructs `b`, for context
+   radii 0..=5.
+
+6. **Ratio bounds and ratio==1 iff equal** (`src/text/mod.rs`,
+   `hegel_ratio_bounds_and_equality`). `TextDiff::ratio()` is in
+   `0..=1`; exactly `1.0` iff the inputs are equal (token counts are far
+   below 2^24 so the f32 comparison is exact).
+
+7. **Text-level reconstruction** (`src/text/mod.rs`,
+   `hegel_textdiff_changes_reconstruct_inputs`). For
+   `diff_lines`/`diff_words`/`diff_chars` on full-Unicode and
+   line-structured text, concatenating Equal+Delete change values yields
+   `old` and Equal+Insert yields `new` (also proves the tokenizers
+   partition their input).
+
+8. **Change index consistency** (`src/text/mod.rs`,
+   `hegel_iter_changes_index_consistency`). `iter_all_changes` walks old
+   indices `0..old_len()` and new indices `0..new_len()` in order; index
+   presence matches the tag; each change value equals the token at its
+   index.
+
+9. **Unified-diff apply roundtrip** (`src/udiff.rs`,
+   `hegel_unified_diff_apply_roundtrip`). An independent, hand-written
+   unified-diff applier (hunk-header parsing per the POSIX diff spec,
+   ' '/'-'/'+' lines, `\ No newline at end of file` hints) applies
+   `unified_diff(alg, old, new, radius, None)` to `old` and must produce
+   `new`, for all algorithms and context radii 0..=4, including
+   `\r\n` lines and missing final newlines. Exercises diffing,
+   `grouped_ops`, hunk-header arithmetic and newline hints end to end.
+
+10. **Remapper concat roundtrip** (`src/utils.rs`,
+    `hegel_utils_diffs_concat_to_inputs`). `utils::diff_chars` /
+    `diff_words` / `diff_lines` yield slices of the original strings whose
+    Equal+Delete concatenation is `old` and Equal+Insert concatenation is
+    `new`; full-Unicode inputs exercise `SliceRemapper`'s byte-offset
+    arithmetic on multi-byte characters. *Found the panic consequence of
+    the bug.*
+
+Generator notes: lone `\r` line terminators are deliberately excluded from
+the *udiff* text generator because `similar` reuses token values verbatim in
+patch output, and a lone-`\r` "line" produces output no line-based patch
+parser can split (values then don't end at physical patch lines). That is a
+representation limitation of the unified diff format itself, not a crate
+bug, so it is excluded by construction rather than pinned.
+
+## Test results
+
+- `cargo test`: **91 passed, 2 failed** — the two failures are the
+  deterministic KNOWN FAILURE pins for the real bug below. All 10
+  properties pass. Doc tests: 21 passed.
+- Liveness verified: temporarily inverting the assertions in properties 1
+  and 9 made hegel report shrunk minimal counterexamples (both shrink to
+  empty inputs); reverted. The `.hegel/` failure database was removed
+  afterwards and added to `.gitignore`.
+- Exploratory 10x run: all properties were run once with
+  `test_cases = 1000` (verified live via a case counter, since the suite
+  is fast enough that wall-clock time barely changes) — no additional
+  failures; settings reverted to the default.
+
+## Suspected bugs
+
+**One real bug (two pinned symptoms): `Algorithm::Lcs` and
+`Algorithm::Hunt` emit a spurious zero-length `Delete` op when both input
+ranges are empty, which makes public `utils::diff_*` functions panic on
+empty strings.**
+
+- Repro (ops level): `capture_diff_slices::<u8>(Algorithm::Lcs, &[], &[])`
+  returns `[Delete { old_index: 0, old_len: 0, new_index: 0 }]` instead of
+  `[]`. Same for `Algorithm::Hunt`. Myers, Patience and Histogram return
+  `[]`.
+- Repro (panic): `similar::utils::diff_chars(Algorithm::Lcs, "", "")`
+  panics with `slice out of bounds` at `src/utils.rs:211`
+  (`TextDiffRemapper::iter_slices` → `SliceRemapper::slice(0..0)` returns
+  `None` because the token index list is empty). `diff_words`,
+  `diff_lines` and the Hunt variants panic identically.
+- Root cause: `lcs::diff_deadline_impl` (src/algorithms/lcs.rs:115) and
+  `hunt::diff_deadline_impl` (src/algorithms/hunt.rs:158) check
+  `is_empty_range(&new_range)` first and unconditionally emit
+  `d.delete(old_range.start, old_range.len(), new_range.start)` — with
+  *both* ranges empty that is a zero-length delete. Compare
+  `myers.rs:925` and `histogram.rs:192`, which have an explicit
+  both-empty guard that returns without emitting anything.
+- Also violates the self-diff property (`diff(x, x)` should be all-Equal)
+  and the "no empty ops" well-formedness for these two algorithms.
+- Verified against the pristine upstream 3.1.1 tree
+  (`upstream-cache/_v3/similar`, same commit `0210f53`): the source is
+  identical, so this is an upstream bug, not an artifact of this working
+  copy.
+- Pinned by two deterministic (non-generative) failing tests:
+  - `src/common.rs`:
+    `common::pbt::hegel_known_failure_lcs_hunt_empty_inputs_spurious_delete`
+    (reports both offending algorithms in one assertion).
+  - `src/utils.rs`:
+    `utils::pbt::hegel_known_failure_lcs_hunt_empty_diff_chars_panics`
+    (the user-facing panic).
+- Sibling properties exclude exactly the `Lcs`/`Hunt` × both-inputs-empty
+  case, each exclusion commented with a reference to the canonical pinned
+  test. No fix was applied, per instructions.
+
+## Unsound properties abandoned
+
+- **"ops == [] for equal inputs" / "exactly one Equal op"** — considered
+  asserting that a self-diff produces a single merged Equal op, but
+  nothing in the docs promises op granularity, only tags and coverage;
+  weakened to "all ops are Equal" plus ratio == 1.0.
+- **Ratio equality across algorithms** — the algorithms legitimately find
+  different amounts of matching content (Myers is minimal, Histogram/
+  Patience prefer readable anchors), so `ratio` is not
+  algorithm-independent; only the bounds/iff-equal property is sound.
+- **Unified-diff roundtrip for lone-`\r` line endings** — abandoned as a
+  *property* (see generator notes above): the unified diff text format
+  cannot faithfully represent a lone-`\r` terminated line as one patch
+  line, so no applier can be a sound oracle there. Not pinned as a bug
+  because it is a limitation of the format, though upstream may want to
+  document it.
+
+## Skill feedback
+
+- The "verify the tests are live" and "one exploratory high-count run"
+  steps were both cheap and worthwhile here; the case-counter trick was
+  needed to confirm the 10x run was real because this suite is so fast
+  that wall-clock time barely changes — the reference's "passing tests
+  print nothing extra" note could mention timing as an unreliable signal
+  and suggest a quick counter/verbosity check when a 10x run looks
+  identical to the 1x run.
+- `cargo add --dev hegeltest` failing on MSRV and the `--ignore-rust-version`
+  retry are covered by the Rust reference Setup section; it worked exactly
+  as documented.
+- The skill's advice to put shared generators somewhere reachable would
+  have helped: with inline `#[cfg(test)]` modules in a single crate,
+  `pub(crate)` test-support modules (`common::pbt_support`,
+  `text::pbt`) worked well and kept tests next to the code they test, but
+  it took a moment to settle on; a sentence in the Rust reference about
+  sharing generators between *inline unit-test modules* (as opposed to
+  the existing `src/` vs `tests/` note) would save that.
+- The "construct degenerate cases exactly" guidance paid off in reverse:
+  the bug lived at the most degenerate input (both empty), reached only
+  because generators deliberately did not require non-empty input —
+  "Don't Require Non-Empty by Default" found this bug.
